{"step_index":748,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T23:09:30Z","input_tokens":3001,"cache_read_tokens":204687,"output_tokens":865,"thinking":"The error indicates a permission issue, specifically a denial of deletion. This points directly to the Firestore security rules. Examination of the rules confirms that deletions are explicitly disallowed for submissions within quizzes. Therefore, the \"Clear Students\" function's inability to delete is expected.\n\n\nThe Firestore rule restricting deletions directly causes the \"Clear Students\" function's failure. Allowing deletion in the `submissions` rule is required for this function to work, updating the rule to permit `delete` or allowing `write` for `submissions` under a quiz.\n\nThe modal confirmation for the clear students action requires specific text and buttons. The modal must display the text \"Are you sure this is what you want?\" with \"Yes\" and \"No\" buttons, closing on \"No\" and triggering the Firestore clear on \"Yes.\" Auto submissions should default to off, reflected in `teacher.html`, Firestore, and the student interface, with appropriate UI indications. Non-major Patch 1.0.17 requires an update entry in `HISTORY.md`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"firestore batch delete collection web javascript compat"}}]}
{"step_index":749,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T23:09:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T07:09:41+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T07:09:45+08:00\nThe search for \"firestore batch delete collection web javascript compat\" returned the following summary:\nTo delete an entire Cloud Firestore collection using the **Web Namespaced / Compat API (Version 8 syntax)**, you cannot delete the collection directly with a single command[1]. Instead, you must fetch documents in batches and use write batches (`db.batch()`) to delete them iteratively (since Firestore batches are limited to a maximum of 500 writes at a time)[2][3].\n\nHere is a robust helper function using the **v8 compat syntax** (`firebase.firestore()`)[2]:\n\n```javascript\n/**\n * Deletes a Firestore collection in batches using the Web v8 compat syntax.\n * \n * @param {firebase.firestore.Firestore} db - The Firestore compat instance\n * @param {string} collectionPath - The path to the collection (e.g., 'users/123/orders')\n * @param {number} batchSize - Number of documents to delete per batch (max 500)\n */\nasync function deleteCollection(db, collectionPath, batchSize) {\n  const collectionRef = db.collection(collectionPath);\n  const query = collectionRef.orderBy('__name__').limit(batchSize);\n\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    deleteQueryBatch(db, query, batchSize, resolve, reject);\n  });\n}\n\nasync function deleteQueryBatch(db, query, batchSize, resolve, reject) {\n  try {\n    const snapshot = await query.get();\n\n    // If there are no documents left, we are done\n    if (snapshot.size === 0) {\n      resolve();\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Otherwise, delete documents in a batch\n    const batch = db.batch();\n    snapshot.docs.forEach((doc) => {\n      batch.delete(doc.ref);\n    });\n\n    await batch.commit();\n\n    // Recurse on the next batch to avoid memory issues and handle large collections\n    process.nextTick\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      deleteQueryBatch(db, query, batchSize, resolve, reject);\n    }, 0);\n\n  } catch (error) {\n    reject(error);\n  }\n}\n\n// --- How to call it ---\n// const db = firebase.firestore();\n// deleteCollection(db, 'your-collection-name', 100)\n//   .then(() => console.log('Collection deleted successfully'))\n//   .catch((error) => console.error('Error deleting collection: ', error));\n```\n\n### Key Considerations:\n1. **Subcollections:** This script deletes the documents *inside* the specified collection. If those documents contain hidden subcollections, they will not be automatically deleted[4][5] and will need to be cleaned up separately.\n2. **Client-side vs. Server-side:** Doing this on the web client exposes your database read/write traffic and is subject to security rules. For large collections, it is strongly recommended to run deletion scripts via a trusted environment (like Node.js with `firebase-admin`)[3] or use the Firebase CLI command (`firebase firestore:delete`)[6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEJQZirxiOCqxgDKJuRMVW2RE9gdyl2ev_j-k8hIr0D-vuKxCMMtnfF92dL6JGO9UjSP9NIGk09OqsZRIDsIuAXKHyb7ki2YtqqQD98JNjee18uRXpn-VF067RV0CEr627GEs1glMf5rrZuUMy_7A7stpLl4l2RhCpxxTYuybPU3EazkYhgDHsTGORhhVC0tvSOu1z1C94iOw==)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFeq39kxJbkWgHM3df3EH2YRkXLWQGZNwQwSGg2Tza9cbRg_p4fLvb3kmDqyuM2mdzJ6t87UCTIox_6YpBE6G5mw5nCiHifRcPC1tTVBAxyufQr4mnrvzxtw0o_E4HHQNMHDNe-zfqIURhLXWh_I37dk70XPlAuL5s1XZwLv7BILgBpZ3GQlr4xoZXohrtHI6Ve)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGmIw58O-jBoW_6fU_YAfEnzjsSCi0L95C3SgpUaCAUAR2eDD8LjEsXbju2s1MVt3SRJAyfxfnXQ4RzyamltJyuPk605YFd8ap5hsIpgJRP3dD1P44SodklUDjGhSM0UAwrKXdYCpclEIP_EpTcrD-KpxSddkbcGkqy7UpBDEIQiiviWxNwQ5YvmnMh7hw5yya9Cg==)\n[4] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHmIF_F7T6ktMpKmBcZfdgIw7Gd6afhuUrzNnnqPfsYEI6f6wmWKV_l0fDsf0lsMZjbE2Tm_Tf1B9QM9ixScnmccHu5E3CfuvUUhH931TcC3wbEIPsT9MI2bACgMLfheO6a7GDny09Wge02Ql_Uv-IHZodne5TPGpK6SHDfTUY1g724tX1pl2xNgPxCA1erKO57mMgb6x9b3u6D1MxI0Z-beVg0Z6tti4RUWa7zhvMIhsf3SA==)\n[5] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGmEGPI5i1oM9Ad1cUUUvmz4eBJT2H01nAEHggnzklIeiWrnZ9ph7WKw8yim-Ib2gmrkDkWadBHB7LEi6GTvsJ9eOv-YUHjcyvnLOdbscX3tCa8S97zbqrpAt-wTL5Ef2lRXW0fS7B2CK0OeDjJx7X5WZE28Jr8a_VflCRzgR0XFwk=)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFeq39kxJbkWgHM3df3EH2YRkXLWQGZNwQwSGg2Tza9cbRg_p4fLvb3kmDqyuM2mdzJ6t87UCTIox_6YpBE6G5mw5nCiHifRcPC1tTVBAxyufQr4mnrvzxtw0o_E4HHQNMHDNe-zfqIURhLXWh_I37dk70XPlAuL5s1XZwLv7BILgBpZ3GQlr4xoZXohrtHI6Ve)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":750,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T23:09:45Z","input_tokens":2686,"cache_read_tokens":207701,"output_tokens":2381,"thinking":"Initial observation: The code snippet in `teacher.html` utilizes batch delete to remove submissions from a quiz. This operation requires a specific Firestore security rule to permit the deletion. The relevant rule should be configured to allow delete operations under the path `/quizzes/{quizId}/submissions/{subId}`.\n\n\nThe provided code reveals the implementation of a \"Clear Students\" button and a confirmation modal for quiz submissions. Clicking the button triggers a modal asking for confirmation before initiating a batch delete operation on student submissions. This delete action is the same as the one which requires the security rule to allow deletions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan to set auto submissions to OFF by default, add a Clear Students button with the exact 'Are you sure this is what you want?' confirmation modal (Yes/No), and purge existing test submissions.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan: Default Auto Submissions to OFF, Clear Students Button & Confirmation Modal\n\n## 1. Overview of Requested Changes\n\n1. **Default Auto Submissions to OFF**:\n   - In [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html), initialize `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz = false`.\n   - Update UI `#btn-auto-rec` to show `OFF` by default.\n   - Update live Firestore document `quizzes/active` setting `autoRecordQuiz` to `false`.\n\n2. **Remove All Test Subjects (Submissions)**:\n   - Purge all test submissions currently residing in `quizzes/active/submissions`.\n   - > [!IMPORTANT]\n     > To allow the teacher portal to delete submissions from Firestore, the Firestore security rule for `submissions` must include `delete`:\n     > ```\n     > match /quizzes/{quizId}/submissions/{subId} {\n     >   allow read, create, delete: if true;\n     >   allow update: if false;\n     > }\n     > ```\n\n3. **Clear Students Button & Confirmation Modal in [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)**:\n   - Add a **Clear Students** button inside the Submissions tab card header.\n   - When clicked, display a confirmation modal with the exact prompt:\n     `Are you sure this is what you want?`\n   - Provide two action buttons: **Yes** and **No**:\n     - **No**: Closes the modal with no action.\n     - **Yes**: Deletes all student submissions from Firestore (`quizzes/{quizId}/submissions`) in batches and closes the modal.\n     - If Firestore rules block deletion, displays an informative prompt to add `delete` to the rules.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Technical Implementation Details\n\n### 2.1 [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)\n- **Settings Default**:\n  - `let settingsState = { ..., autoRecordQuiz: false };`\n- **Markup in `#view-sub`**:\n  ```html\n  <div class=\"top\">\n    <h2>Completed Students</h2>\n    <div class=\"row\" style=\"gap:8px\">\n      <span id=\"sub-count-badge\" class=\"badge\">0 Done</span>\n      <button id=\"clear-sub-btn\" class=\"danger\" type=\"button\" style=\"padding:4px 10px;font-size:0.85rem\">Clear Students</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  ```\n- **Confirmation Modal Markup**:\n  ```html\n  <div id=\"confirm-modal\" class=\"warn hide\">\n    <div class=\"card\" style=\"max-width:380px;text-align:center\">\n      <h2 style=\"margin:0 0 16px;font-size:1.15rem\">Are you sure this is what you want?</h2>\n      <div class=\"row\" style=\"justify-content:center;gap:12px\">\n        <button id=\"modal-yes-btn\" class=\"danger\" type=\"button\" style=\"padding:10px 24px\">Yes</button>\n        <button id=\"modal-no-btn\" class=\"sec\" type=\"button\" style=\"padding:10px 24px\">No</button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  ```\n- **Modal Event Logic**:\n  - `$('clear-sub-btn').onclick = () => $('confirm-modal').classList.remove('hide');`\n  - `$('modal-no-btn').onclick = () => $('confirm-modal').classList.add('hide');`\n  - `$('modal-yes-btn').onclick = async () => { ... batch delete submissions ... $('confirm-modal').classList.add('hide'); }`\n\n### 2.2 Firestore & Template Sync\n- Update `quizzes/active` setting `autoRecordQuiz` to `false`.\n- Synchronize `quizzes/template` with the latest `index.html`.\n\n### 2.3 [HISTORY.md](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md)\n- Append Non-Major Patch 1.0.17 documenting the default OFF setting, Clear Students button, and exact confirmation modal per Rule 1.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency & Ripple Effect Analysis\n\n| Component / Flow | Dependency Type | Potential Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Auto Submission Default | `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz` | Student quiz loads in manual mode | When `autoRecordQuiz === false`, student results display the manual download and copy buttons as expected. |\n| Submissions Deletion | Firestore `batch.delete()` | Security rule denial (`PERMISSION_DENIED`) | Catch error and display clear notification to update security rule to `allow read, create, delete: if true;`. |\n| Confirmation Modal | Modal overlay (`.warn`) | Layout overflow | Reuses existing `.warn` fixed overlay styles already verified across both themes. |\n| Original File | Untouchable asset | Rule violation | `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` kept untouched per Rules 2 & 12. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification Plan (Rules 3 & 10)\n\n1. **Default State Verification**:\n   - Verify `teacher.html` loads with `Auto Record Quiz` toggle set to `OFF`.\n   - Verify `quizzes/active` in Firestore has `settings.autoRecordQuiz === false`.\n2. **Clear Students Button & Modal Verification**:\n   - In `teacher.html`, switch to `Submissions` tab and click **Clear Students**.\n   - Verify modal appears with the exact heading: *\"Are you sure this is what you want?\"* and buttons *\"Yes\"* and *\"No\"*.\n   - Verify clicking **No** closes the modal without changes.\n   - Verify clicking **Yes** executes batch deletion on `quizzes/{quizId}/submissions`.\n3. **Rule 9 Zero-Comment Compliance**:\n   - Verify zero comments or docstrings in `teacher.html`.\n4. **Original File Integrity**:\n   - Confirm `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` remains untouched.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
